@page "/docs/theming"
<PageTitle>Theming - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Theming</h1>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">CSS variables</BzBadge>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">light / dark / system</BzBadge>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">8 styles</BzBadge>
        </div>
        <p>Every color in Blaizio is a semantic CSS variable such as <code>--primary</code>, mapped to the Tailwind utilities the components use (<code>bg-primary</code>, <code>text-primary-foreground</code>, ...). Change a variable and every component follows, in both light and dark mode. For ready-made light, dark and system pickers, see the <a href="docs/components/theme-switcher">Theme Switcher</a> component, and to compose a whole look visually, use <a href="themes">Themes</a>.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Convention</h2>
        <p>Tokens come in <code>background</code> / <code>foreground</code> pairs. The base token (<code>--primary</code>) is a surface color, and its <code>-foreground</code> partner (<code>--primary-foreground</code>) is the text and icon color used on that surface. The <em>background</em> suffix is left off, so a component paints <code>bg-primary text-primary-foreground</code> and both values flip together when the mode changes.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Theme tokens</h2>
        <p>Theme-wide values live in one file, while each component keeps its own structural look:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><b>The tokens file.</b> When <code>blaizio add</code> wires your project, it creates <code>Styles/app.css</code>, which holds the Tailwind input, the <code>:root</code>/<code>.dark</code> values and the map from tokens to utilities. The file is yours, so edit the values directly. The CLI only keeps the imports in sync and patches values when you run <code>apply</code>.</li>
            <li><b>Each component carries its own look.</b> <code>add</code> copies components with the structural styling of the style you picked inlined in their classes. Change a component's look in its own file, and theme-wide values in the tokens file.</li>
            <li><b>This docs site is the exception.</b> It loads all eight styles as stylesheets so you can switch between them at runtime. A real project installs one style's components and switches style with <code>blaizio apply</code>.</li>
        </ul>
        <BzTable ContainerClass="rounded-lg border" Class="text-sm">
                <BzTableHeader>
                    <BzTableRow Class="bg-muted/50 text-start">
                        <BzTableHead>Token</BzTableHead>
                        <BzTableHead>Used for</BzTableHead>
                    </BzTableRow>
                </BzTableHeader>
                <BzTableBody Class="text-muted-foreground [&_code]:text-foreground">
                    <BzTableRow><BzTableCell><code>background</code> / <code>foreground</code></BzTableCell><BzTableCell>The page itself and its default text.</BzTableCell></BzTableRow>
